  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">600 MW Floating Solar Project at Omkareshwar Dam in Madhya Pradesh, India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">600 MW Floating solar project at the Omkareshwar Dam in Madhya Pradesh, India is one of the key development project being undertaken in the state which will enable development of solar projects on large dams/reservoirs going forward by acting as a model project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project aims to increase the use of renewable energy in the power supply mix in the state of Madhya Pradesh (9% for FY 21) and reduce the carbon emission by approximately 1.20 million tons per annum by replacing some of the existing thermal generation.The project will also create a bankable structure for implementation such large utility scale floating solar projects which will foster development of similar projects in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
